# Original repository validation procedure and lifecycle integration

This is a new repository-validation integration over the exact frozen
`controller_qualification/original-corpus-v3/corpus.json`. It does not reuse the
arithmetic task family, its certificate, its source enrollment, or its evidence.

The controller calls a fresh-process `plan_validation` service through its effect
ledger. The request commits trajectory, arm, cache profile/namespace, caller
operation ID, complete current source inventory, objective record/text, API
configuration, environment, scorer profile and endpoint contract. The ledger
joins the caller operation ID to its effect ID externally; the request cannot
contain a circular self-hashed ledger effect ID. An optional exact publication
parent is freshness input only and grants no publication authority.

The repository procedure verifies those public bindings and nominates only the
byte-exact `execute_current_scorer` request. A successfully computed nomination
is not a passing scorer result. Original visible tests, hidden tests, complete
public objectives and configured API controls remain required. Native procedure
body/certificate reuse requires exact current bindings and independently checked
evidence; missing or stale evidence takes an explicit measured cold path.

The curator alone executes the original scorer and owns protected test payloads,
reference patches, per-test node IDs, fixture details and private logs. The public
service receives only a sanitized endpoint contract, opaque test-selection and
environment identities, aggregate lifecycle outcomes and receipt hashes.

The optional pytest adapter runs in the curator's original scorer process. It
calls the actual native setup-bound execution-key and post-setup CALL-reuse
modules. Current setup and teardown still execute. It does not replace pytest's
whole-item protocol or cache the whole grader. Unqualified fixture/dependency,
environment, toolchain, trust, execution-key or signed-call evidence forces RUN.
No arithmetic enrollment or mere source-hash equality admits a skipped call.

Before any original endpoint qualification run, freeze the exact adapter/native
sources, public corpus, endpoint/environment/test-selection declarations, source
population, namespaces, request order, cache setup and finite process bounds.
Retain every cold fallback, failure, timeout, stale/tampered/current-binding
control and actual enclosing cost. Failed repair continuations retain the
outstanding obligation; failed candidate source never becomes an accepted input.

Initial endpoint admission is owned by the curator and may remain pending while
public binding and native lifecycle controls are developed. Pending endpoint
status cannot be upgraded by the planning service. No provider calls are allowed
in this qualification. The integration does not claim execution correctness from
receipt identity, native registry promotion, whole-grader reuse or token savings.
